From e9ff73234e8af0c10583942f6c5830585ee90277 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fable <fable@local>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:21:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] W0-10 PR-2b: free vehicles on deployment end (+ transfer
 terminal states)

Root-cause fix so the one-open-RigVehicle-per-vehicle invariant (index C, PR-2c)
becomes true and creatable. deployments/[id]/end now closes the rig's open
rig_vehicles rows, freeing each vehicle for its next deployment; previously they
were left open forever on the ended rig (no path could close them), which both
blocked reuse and would trip index C. A backfill migration closes historical
ended-rig rows (removedAt = rig.endedAt).

Four-agent review caught a regression in the first cut: unconditionally closing
the rows bricked in-flight vehicle transfers (accept's stillPresent guard needs
removedAt IS NULL). Fixed by excluding vehicles with a PENDING outbound transfer
from the end close-out AND the backfill, and by closing the source rows on the
decline/cancel terminal paths when the source rig already ended (mirrors the
existing ended-rig kit-item reconciliation) so no vehicle strands.

Also adds 23505/P2002 -> friendly 409 translation to the vehicle/deployment/
operator writers (dormant until the indexes ship; removes the raw-500 edge).

Index C itself is deferred to PR-2c: it is created only AFTER this close-out
fix is deployed and confirmed live (writer-before-constraint ordering), with a
prod pre-flight that must also catch active/active duplicates the backfill can't.
